    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d339">

                <pb facs="0447" n="352" sameAs="frus:frus1936v04/pg352"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/8346</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 778</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-10-15">October 15, 1936</date>.<lb/>[Received November
                        16.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith a
                    copy of despatch No. 66 of October 9, 1936, from the Consulate at Tsinan<anchor
                        n="36" xml:id="d339-f1"/> in which Consul Allison reports the opinion of the
                    Secretary of the German Embassy in Tokyo to the effect that Japan is not ready
                    to engage in war at this time for the following reasons: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>The economic and financial situation in Japan is extremely
                            serious.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>The Japanese Army is not in sufficiently good condition.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>Japan has no international agreements which would be of assistance in
                            case of war.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Ambassador:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">George R.
                            Merrell, Jr.</hi></signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">First Secretary
                        of Embassy</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
